From: Dynamic Devices BSP Maintainers <support@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] optee: retain Foundries security and PKCS#11 delta

Forward-port the six Foundries-specific changes from the 4.4.0+fio-imx
branch onto NXP's lf-6.12.49_2.2.0 OP-TEE baseline. The two additional
Foundries RPMB fixes are already present upstream in this NXP baseline.
Extend the HUK weak-stub exclusion to CFG_MX95, whose strong implementation
is supplied by the ELE driver, so the original fail-closed intent covers the
new SoC family.

Original Foundries commits:
- 7ee0f456d PKCS#11 TA UUID separation from SKS
- caff966a2 PKCS#11 token description device ID
- 0599f2a12 remove the i.MX HUK weak stub
- 94aabbc53 PKCS#11 import of pre-allocated secure-element keys
- 80e3ff95f SE050 ECC/RSA key import
- a475b6048 prohibit derived SCP03 keys until RPMB is ready

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Foundries-specific integration]

